1. Definitions
1.1. Software

"Software" means the software identified by the relevant copyright or license notice as being distributed under this License, including its source files, executable forms, documentation, and other materials included as part of the licensed work.

1.2. Source Code

"Source Code" means the preferred form of a work for making modifications to it. Source Code includes, as applicable:

(a) human-readable source files and scripts;

(b) build systems, build files, configuration files, dependency specifications, and installation and deployment scripts;

(c) interface definitions, schemas, templates, and other materials necessary to understand or reproduce the work's functionality;

(d) documentation and technical specifications necessary to understand, build, modify, test, or maintain the work; and

(e) the corresponding source-level materials for modifications incorporated into a distributed Derivative Work.

Source Code does not require the inclusion of independently developed tools or materials that are neither part of the work nor necessary to build or modify it. Third-party materials are subject to Section 4.7.

1.3. Derivative Work

"Derivative Work" means a work based upon or incorporating protectable expression from the Software, including a modification, adaptation, translation, port, or other work that qualifies as a derivative or adapted work under applicable copyright principles.

A work does not become a Derivative Work solely because it interoperates with, communicates with, or is independently developed for use alongside the Software.

1.4. Author and Rights Holder

"Author" means countryside99, identified as the original author of the Software.

"Relevant Rights Holder" means the Author or another person or entity that owns or is authorized to license the particular rights at issue.

1.5. Licensee

"You" or "Licensee" means any person or entity exercising rights granted under this License.

1.6. Distribution

"Distribution" means transferring, publishing, supplying, or otherwise making a copy of the Software or a Derivative Work available to another person or entity, whether through downloads, repositories, physical media, application distribution, or other means.

Distribution does not include merely retaining a private copy or making private modifications that are not provided to another person or entity.

1.7. Commercial Use

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software or a Derivative Work undertaken for, on behalf of, or in support of a commercial, business, professional, or revenue-generating activity, or for the purpose of obtaining a direct or indirect commercial or business advantage.

Commercial Use includes, without limitation:

(a) selling, renting, leasing, licensing for consideration, monetizing, or otherwise commercially exploiting the Software or a Derivative Work;

(b) incorporating, bundling, embedding, or distributing the Software as part of a commercial product, service, platform, or offering;

(c) using or deploying the Software in the operations of a commercial business or enterprise, including internal development, testing, evaluation, production, administration, and maintenance;

(d) using the Software to provide paid services, hosted services, software-as-a-service (SaaS), commercial APIs, consulting, or other services provided for commercial advantage;

(e) using the Software to perform professional work or provide deliverables on behalf of a commercial client or employer, including where the Licensee receives no separate payment for using the Software;

(f) using the Software to support advertising, monetization, customer acquisition, commercial data processing, or other business operations;

(g) using the Software or its Source Code to train, fine-tune, evaluate, benchmark, or develop an artificial intelligence or machine-learning system intended for Commercial Use; and

(h) permitting, facilitating, or enabling another person to undertake any of the foregoing activities using the Software or a Derivative Work.

Commercial Use does not require the receipt of payment or the generation of a profit. An activity may constitute Commercial Use even if it is free of charge, experimental, preliminary, charitable in part, or described as research or evaluation.

1.8. Non-Commercial Purpose

"Non-Commercial Purpose" means a purpose that is not Commercial Use under Section 1.7.

Examples include personal study, private experimentation, hobby projects, and genuinely non-commercial educational activities undertaken independently of commercial operations and without the purpose of providing commercial advantage.

An activity does not qualify as a Non-Commercial Purpose merely because no payment is made for the particular use. The actual purpose and context of the activity determine whether it is permitted.

1.9. Attribution

"Attribution" means a clear and reasonably prominent identification of the Author, preservation of applicable original copyright and license notices, and identification of modifications where required by this License.

