(d) use and execute the Software for permitted Non-Commercial Purposes; and

(e) distribute the Software and Derivative Works in accordance with Sections 3 and 4.

The rights granted are limited to those necessary to exercise the permissions expressly stated in this License.

2.2. Attribution Requirements

Every distributed copy of the Software or a Derivative Work must:

(a) preserve all original copyright notices and license notices included with the Software;

(b) identify countryside99 as the Author of the original Software;

(c) include a complete copy of this License or accompany the work with a complete, directly accessible copy as permitted by Section 9;

(d) identify modifications in a reasonably prominent manner; and

(e) avoid suggesting that the Author created, approved, or endorses modifications made by another person.

Attribution must not be removed, concealed, or materially altered in a manner that misrepresents authorship or ownership.

2.3. No Commercial Rights

No Commercial Use is authorized under this License. Any permission for Commercial Use must be expressly granted in a separate written authorization by the Relevant Rights Holder.

2.4. Reserved Rights and Patents

Except for the express copyright permissions granted in this License, all rights are reserved by the applicable rights holders.

No express patent license is granted under this License. Any patent rights, if applicable, remain subject to the rights and permissions independently available from the relevant patent holder. Nothing in this Section excludes a right or limitation that cannot lawfully be excluded.

No trademark or branding license is granted except as necessary to preserve factual attribution and identify the Software.

2.5. Termination and Revocability

The license is subject to the termination provisions in Section 5. It is not independently revocable at will while the Licensee remains in compliance, except where otherwise permitted by applicable law or expressly agreed in writing by the Relevant Rights Holder.

3. Strict Non-Commercial Restriction
3.1. Prohibition

You must not engage in Commercial Use of the Software, its Source Code, or any Derivative Work.

This prohibition applies whether the Software is modified or unmodified, whether the activity generates revenue, and whether the Software is used directly or indirectly to support a commercial activity.

3.2. Prohibited Activities

Without limiting Section 3.1, You must not:

(a) sell, monetize, rent, or commercially license the Software or a Derivative Work;

(b) incorporate the Software into a commercial product, paid application, commercial platform, or revenue-generating service;

(c) use the Software in commercial business operations, including internal business testing, development, evaluation, or deployment;

(d) use the Software to provide a paid service, SaaS offering, commercial API, or other service intended to provide commercial advantage;

(e) use the Software in professional work performed for a commercial employer, client, or undertaking;

(f) use the Software or its Source Code to develop an AI or machine-learning system intended for Commercial Use; or

(g) authorize, facilitate, or knowingly enable another person to engage in any prohibited activity through access, copies, or services supplied by You.

3.3. Free-of-Charge Activities

Providing the Software without charge does not make an otherwise commercial activity permissible.

Likewise, the absence of direct payment does not permit internal business use, unpaid work for a commercial organization, or activities that support commercial operations.

3.4. Permitted Activities

Subject to all other terms of this License, permitted activities include:

(a) personal study and private experimentation;

(b) hobby projects undertaken for personal purposes;

(c) educational exercises conducted for genuinely non-commercial educational purposes;

(d) private modification and testing for personal learning; and

(e) distribution of compliant copies or Derivative Works for Non-Commercial Purposes.

These examples are illustrative and do not override the definition of Commercial Use in Section 1.7.

3.5. Separate Written Authorization

Commercial Use is permitted only if the Relevant Rights Holder expressly authorizes that use in writing. The authorization must be sufficiently clear to identify the scope of the commercial permission granted.

Permission from a person who does not own or control the relevant rights is insufficient.

4. ShareTheSource: Mandatory Copyleft
4.1. Same-License Requirement

Every Derivative Work distributed by You must be licensed under the exact license identified as the Attribution Non-Commercial ShareTheSource License, Version 1.0 (ANCS-1.0).

You must not impose additional terms that remove, weaken, or conflict with the rights and restrictions established by ANCS-1.0.

This requirement applies to the Derivative Work to the extent that it is based upon or incorporates the Software and is within the scope of the applicable rights held or controlled by the Relevant Rights Holder.

4.2. Complete Corresponding Source Code

Whenever You distribute the Software or a Derivative Work, You must make the complete corresponding Source Code for the distributed version available to every Recipient.

The Source Code must:

(a) include all modifications incorporated into the distributed version;

(b) be provided in the preferred form for making modifications;

(c) include applicable build files, scripts, configuration files, dependency specifications, and documentation required to build, modify, or maintain the distributed version;

(d) be provided in a readable, unencrypted, and unobstructed form, without technical measures that prevent recipients from accessing or modifying it;

(e) include all applicable original notices, attribution, modification notices, and a copy of ANCS-1.0; and

(f) be made available at the time of distribution, without a separate charge for access to the Source Code.

4.3. Method of Providing Source Code

You may satisfy Section 4.2 by:

(a) including the complete Source Code with the distributed copy; or

(b) providing a working, direct, and reasonably accessible link to a repository or download location containing the complete corresponding Source Code.

A public repository, including a GitHub repository, is the recommended method.

The Source Code must be accessible to every Recipient without discriminatory access restrictions, mandatory payment, or unnecessary registration requirements.

A link to an incomplete, unavailable, private, or materially obstructed repository does not satisfy this requirement.

4.4. Private Modifications

You may modify the Software for private use without publishing those modifications, provided that the modified Software and its Source Code are not distributed or otherwise made available to another person or entity.

The mere creation, retention, or private use of a modification does not trigger a publication or source-sharing obligation under this License.

If You subsequently distribute the modified Software or a Derivative Work, Sections 4.1 and 4.2 apply to that distribution.

4.5. Modification Notices

You must clearly identify material modifications to the Software in the distributed Source Code or accompanying documentation.

You must preserve original copyright and license notices and must not represent Your modifications as original work created by countryside99.

4.6. Recipients' Rights

You must provide recipients with the rights granted by ANCS-1.0, including the rights to study, modify, and redistribute the Software and Source Code for permitted Non-Commercial Purposes.

You must not impose contractual or technical restrictions that prevent recipients from exercising those rights.

Recipients remain subject to the Non-Commercial restrictions and all other conditions of ANCS-1.0.

4.7. Third-Party Components and Dependencies

This License applies only to rights that the Relevant Rights Holder owns or is authorized to license.

If the Software or a Derivative Work incorporates third-party components, You must:

(a) preserve applicable third-party notices and license terms;

(b) identify separately licensed components where reasonably necessary;

(c) comply with the applicable conditions governing redistribution of those components; and

(d) refrain from representing that ANCS-1.0 grants rights in third-party materials that the Relevant Rights Holder does not control.

You must not knowingly distribute a package in a manner that violates applicable third-party rights.

If a required component cannot lawfully be redistributed, You must not represent that the distributed package contains the complete corresponding source materials unless the applicable obligations can lawfully be satisfied. You must instead exclude or replace the component, obtain the necessary permissions, or refrain from the affected distribution.

Nothing in this License overrides third-party intellectual property rights or grants permission to distribute materials without the necessary authorization.

4.8. Independent Works

This License does not claim ownership over independent works that neither derive from nor incorporate protectable expression from the Software.

Mere interoperability, communication through an interface, or independent development does not automatically make another work a Derivative Work.

Whether a work qualifies as a Derivative Work depends on the applicable rights and circumstances.

5. Termination and Reinstatement
5.1. Termination for Breach

The rights granted under this License terminate automatically upon a material breach of its terms, subject to the cure provisions in this Section and applicable law.

5.2. Notice and Cure

Where a breach is reasonably capable of remedy, the Relevant Rights Holder may provide written notice identifying the breach and allowing thirty (30) calendar days from receipt of the notice to cure it.

If the breach is not cured within that period, the rights granted under this License shall terminate automatically at the end of the cure period, subject to applicable law.

5.3. Serious or Continuing Violations

Where a breach involves intentional Commercial Use, deliberate concealment of required Source Code, repeated violations after notice, or conduct that cannot reasonably be remedied, the Relevant Rights Holder may terminate the rights immediately by written notice, to the extent permitted by applicable law.

Nothing in this Section limits any remedy that must or may lawfully be exercised without prior notice.

5.4. Consequences of Termination

Upon termination, You must immediately cease exercising the rights granted by this License, except to the extent applicable law provides otherwise.

You must cease unauthorized use and distribution, and take reasonable steps to remove or correct unauthorized distributions under Your control.

Termination does not automatically require the destruction of copies held by unrelated recipients who independently obtained rights under this License and remain in compliance with its terms.

5.5. Reinstatement

The Relevant Rights Holder may reinstate the terminated rights through express written authorization identifying the scope of reinstatement.

Unless that authorization expressly states otherwise, reinstatement applies prospectively and does not waive liability or claims arising from an earlier breach.

5.6. Continuing Obligations

Termination does not extinguish claims, liabilities, or remedies arising before termination. Provisions that by their nature are intended to survive termination shall continue to apply to the extent permitted by applicable law.

